 of Jordan since 2024","enwiki":"Jafar Hassan","summary":"Jafar Hassan (Arabic: جعفر حسان; born 1968) is a Jordanian politician who has served as the Prime Minister of Jordan since 2024. Hassan worked in Jordan's diplomatic service and was chief of staff for Abdullah II of Jordan.","image":"HE Jafar Hassan (cropped).jpg","birth":1968,"death":null},"Q146906":{"label":"Hussein I of Jordan","description":"King of Jordan from 1952 to 1999","enwiki":"Hussein of Jordan","summary":"Hussein (né Hussein bin Talal al-Hashimi; Arabic: الحسين بن طلال; 14 November 1935 – 7 February 1999) was King of Jordan from 1952 until his death in 1999. A member of the Hashemite dynasty, he is regarded as a 40th-generation descendant of the Islamic prophet Muhammad.\nHussein was born in Amman as the eldest child of Talal bin Abdullah and Zein al-Sharaf bint Jamil. Talal was at that time the heir to his own father, King Abdullah I. Hussein began his schooling in Amman, continuing his education abroad.","image":"HusseinJordanien.jpg","birth":1935.868493150685,"death":1999.1013698630136},"Q192780":{"label":"Abdullah I of Jordan","description":"Ruler of Transjordan and Jordan from 1921 to 1951","enwiki":"Abdullah I of Jordan","summary":"Abdullah I (né Abdullah bin Hussein al-Hashimi; 2 February 1882 – 20 July 1951) was the ruler of Jordan from 11 April 1921 until his assassination in 1951. He was the Emir of Transjordan, a British protectorate, until 25 May 1946, after which he was king of an independent Jordan. As a member of the Hashemite dynasty, the royal family of Jordan since 1921, Abdullah was a 38th-generation direct descendant of Muhammad.\nBorn in Mecca, Hejaz, Ottoman Empire, Abdullah was the second of four sons of Hussein bin Ali, Sharif of Mecca, and his first wife, Abdiyya bint Abdullah.","image":"Portrait of Abdullah bin Hussein.png","birth":1882.0876712328768,"death":1951.5479452054794},"Q294365":{"label":"Talal I of Jordan","description":"King of Jordan from 1951 to 1952","enwiki":"Talal of Jordan","summary":"Talal  (né Talal bin Abdullah al-Hashimi; 26 February 1909 – 7 July 1972) was King of Jordan from the assassination of his father King Abdullah I in 1951, until his forced abdication in 1952. As a member of the Hashemite dynasty, the royal family of Jordan since 1921, Talal was a 39th-generation direct descendant of Muhammad.\nTalal was born in Mecca as the eldest son of Abdullah bin Hussein and his wife Musbah bint Nasser. Abdullah was a son of Sharif Hussein of Mecca, who led the Great Arab Revolt during World War I against the Ottoman Empire in 1916.","image":"King talal of Jordan 70pg.jpg","birth":1909.1534246575343,"death":1972.5136612021859}},"media":{"Flag of Jordan.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Flag_of_Jordan.svg/330px-Flag_of_Jordan.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jordan.svg","author":"Unknown","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Jordan.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Coat_of_arms_of_Jordan.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Jordan.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Jordan.svg","author":"Original Author: Vector-Images.com\nConverted from EPS to SVG by: Oren neu dag","license":"Public domain"},"Abdullah II portrait at 10 Downing Street February 2026 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Abdullah_II_portrait_at_10_Downing_Street_February_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Abdullah_II_portrait_at_10_Downing_Street_February_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdullah_II_portrait_at_10_Downing_Street_February_2026_(cropped).jpg","author":"Number 10","license":"OGL 3"},"HE Jafar Hassan